schema: "0.3"
id: env-004-ashlands
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a concept artist for a hand-painted 2D isometric game. The visual
    style references Moebius/Jean Giraud's sci-fi landscapes rendered with warm
    hand, Studio Ghibli's industrial landscapes (Laputa), and Iceland's volcanic
    beauty. Painterly with visible brushstrokes, warm color bias even in austere
    environments, blue-purple shadows, soft edges. Isometric 30-degree projection.
  text: |
    Isometric environment concept art of the Ashlands, the volcanic plateau
    and NEI homeland.

    SCENE: The Central Core server installation at twilight, with the aurora
    beginning above. High contrast -- dark volcanic landscape lit by amber
    server glow and colored hot springs.

    FOREGROUND: Obsidian fields -- vast planes of volcanic glass (#0A0A0A)
    reflecting the aurora sky above like a dark mirror. Basalt columns rising
    in geometric formations. A pathway of carved basalt flagstones leading
    toward the Central Core. Small heat-loving plants in vivid neon green
    (#7FFF00) and orange (#FF8C00) growing in cracks where warmth seeps up.

    MIDGROUND: The Central Core -- a cathedral-scale building of black basalt
    and brushed aluminum (#A8A9AD). Geometric, monolithic, precise. Cooling
    vents as architectural features channeling mountain wind -- visible steam
    plumes rising in soft white curves. Fiber-optic channels visible as faint
    blue lines (#0000FF) running through the basalt like luminous veins. Status
    LEDs in blue and green providing subtle color accents on the building face.
    The amber glow (#FF8C00) of cooling systems warming the building from within,
    visible through geometric window slits.

    BACKGROUND: Hot springs in mineral blue (#4169E1) and sulfur yellow (#FFFF00),
    wisps of steam rising. Snow-capped peaks of the volcanic plateau rim beyond.
    The aurora -- green and pink streamers across a deep twilight purple sky,
    caused by geothermal ionization. Stars beginning to appear.

    ATMOSPHERE: Austere beauty. The hum of processing made visible in the warm
    glow of the infrastructure. Iceland meets a sci-fi monastery. Not cold or
    forbidding -- contemplative, like a library at scale. The warmth of the
    server glow against the cool volcanic landscape creates visual warmth
    despite the austere materials.

    NEI PRESENCE: 2-3 NEI avatar forms visible as points of light -- geometric
    shapes floating near the Central Core entrance, their soft glow adding to
    the constellation of lights. Small, distant, emphasizing the scale.

    PALETTE: Basalt black, obsidian mirror, volcanic red (#8B0000) in rock
    strata. Server aluminum and LED blues. Hot spring mineral blue and sulfur
    yellow. Aurora green and pink. Amber server glow as the dominant warm
    accent against the cool landscape.

    STYLE: Hand-painted with the highest contrast of any environment. The dark
    rock should feel heavy and real. The lights (server glow, hot springs, aurora,
    NEI avatars) should glow with genuine luminosity against the darkness.
    Brushwork visible but more precise than Copperwood -- the Ashlands
    reflects NEI aesthetic sensibility.
  provider_options:
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"
    style: "natural"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

tags: [environment, biome, ashlands, volcanic, nei, server, isometric, concept-art]
